In Kubernetes, Liveness Probe and Readiness Probe Startup Probe are health checks used to manage container lifecycle and traffic routing. They serve different purposes:

🔹 Liveness Probe (Is the app alive?)
✅ Purpose:
Checks whether the application inside the container is still running properly.
🔁 What happens if it fails:
Kubernetes restarts the container.

🧠 Use case:
App is stuck or deadlocked
Memory leak causing unresponsiveness
Infinite loop or crash scenario

Example:
livenessProbe:
  httpGet:
    path: /health
    port: 8080
  initialDelaySeconds: 10
  periodSeconds: 5


🔹 Readiness Probe (Is the app ready?)
✅ Purpose:
Checks whether the application is ready to serve traffic.
🔁 What happens if it fails:
Kubernetes removes the pod from the service/load balancer
No restart happens

🧠 Use case:
App is still starting up
Waiting for DB or external service
Under heavy load and temporarily unable to serve requests

Example:
readinessProbe:
  httpGet:
    path: /ready
    port: 8080
  initialDelaySeconds: 5
  periodSeconds: 3

🔹 Startup Probe (Kubernetes)
✅ Purpose:
A Startup Probe is used to determine whether a containerized application has successfully started.

It is especially useful for slow-starting applications.
It delays the activation of liveness and readiness probes until the app is fully initialized.

🔁 What happens if it fails:

Kubernetes will restart the container, just like a liveness probe.
It keeps retrying until the app starts successfully.

🧠 Why Startup Probe is Needed
Without a startup probe:

Liveness probe might kill the container too early
Happens when apps take long time to initialize (e.g., large JVM apps, ML models, DB connections)

👉 Startup probe protects your app during boot time

Example:
startupProbe:
  httpGet:
    path: /startup
    port: 8080
  failureThreshold: 30
  periodSeconds: 10


🔄 How It Works with Other Probes
Startup Probe runs first
Until it succeeds:
❌ Liveness probe is disabled
❌ Readiness probe is disabled

Once it succeeds:
✅ Liveness probe starts
✅ Readiness probe starts

🧠 Simple Analogy
Startup Probe → "Have you woken up?" 🌅
Liveness Probe → "Are you alive?" 🫀
Readiness Probe → "Can you work right now?" 💼
